# Resume by label: a chat request whose visible conversation continues a turn record (9004) is served that record's
# exact tokens, thinking included, then the tokens of its own render after that turn, so a client that drops the
# thinking still finds its kept or stored prompt state by exact prefix, also after a restart. At prepare time, on the
# request thread, the records are indexed afresh from the kept states' keys and the spill tier's in-RAM fields; the
# deepest label whose records hold one set of tokens for the request's call ids wins once its record is unchanged, every
# earlier turn passes the record's checks (reasoning sent back must equal the record's; foreign reasoning must be sent
# every time; a turn whose reasoning was dropped needs its call ids, or 64 visible characters, to prove it was ours) and
# the tokens' sha256 matches. Anything doubtful, or a context that would not fit, is a miss: today's render serves the
# request, never a refusal. The sampling seed follows the served prompt; /v1/messages/count_tokens counts it; /tokenize
# still renders. Rank 0 only. mgllm, 2026-10-07.
# Tests: tests/test_9005_resume.py (CPU; needs TF_GLM_TEST_MODEL_DIR).

